# Harried Spearguard: "When this creature dies, create a 1/1 black Rat creature token with 'This token can't block.'" Bot2
# Lightning Bolts Bot1's Spearguard on turn 2: it dies and Bot1, its controller (not Bot2, who dealt the damage), gets exactly one
# Rat token, a 1/1 black Rat that can't block. The Rat dies to nothing here; Bot2 has no token.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Harried Spearguard
Mountain x5
Mountain x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Harried Spearguard.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Harried Spearguard)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Harried Spearguard
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Rat Token
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Ruby
Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Toughness = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Colors = Black
Bot1.Battlefield.Rat Token.Keywords = CantBlock
